  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Figshare dataset on the genome of <i>Ichthyophonus hoferi</i> shows an early but clear reuse signal: it has been cited once and appears in two documented downstream reuse records. The record also shows open availability through Figshare and OpenAIRE, which supports accessibility for further research.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published in 2017 by Multicellgenome Lab as an openly available dataset, <i>Genome - Ichthyophonus hoferi</i> provides genome assembly and annotation files for this organism, including assembly, gene annotation, predicted transcripts, and predicted peptides. The metadata places the work within biology, genomics, evolutionary biology, computational biology, zoology, and genetics, matching its use as a foundational resource for comparative and evolutionary study.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest impact signal is still modest in volume but meaningful in kind: OpenAlex records one citation, and the reuse graph shows two downstream reuse records, including a journal article and a biomedical article mention indexed by Europe PMC. That pattern suggests the dataset has begun to support scholarly work, with uptake centered in research literature rather than broader public discussion.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citing landscape is concentrated in a single 2025 eLife article on receptor diversity and evolution in close relatives of metazoa. That citation context, together with the dataset\u2019s biological and evolutionary concepts, indicates that the genome resource is being used in comparative questions relevant to protist diversity, marine and coastal ecosystems, and fish biology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Stewardship signals are consistent with long-term accessibility: the dataset is deposited in Figshare, indexed as open in repository registries, and discoverable through OpenAIRE. The record does not show views or downloads in the available DataCite metadata, and public discourse data are unavailable, so the narrative of impact here rests primarily on scholarly reuse and citation rather than attention metrics.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, this is a well-stewarded dataset with early-stage scholarly uptake. Its impact is best described as focused and research-facing: it has already been reused in the literature, and its open repository placement should continue to support future citation and reuse as related evolutionary and genomic studies develop.</p>",
